  "usdkrw": "DEXKOUS is the Federal Reserve H.10 noon New York buying rate. A US close (16:00 ET) falls after that day's noon print and after the Seoul session of the same calendar date, so KRW NAV uses the next print dated after the session. A KRW investor's actual conversion happens in Seoul hours (KST = ET+13/14); the next-print rule is an observable, no-look-ahead proxy, not a quote the investor could trade at."
